WEBVTT

NOTE
Draft captions for the planned portfolio edit. Re-time and reconcile every cue after the final audio lock. This file is not evidence that a video was recorded.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Most notes fail before the first word:
what should I call this, and where should it go?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Unfiled saves the thought first.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Then it shows where it landed,
what changed, and how to undo it.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000
The result is a normal, usable note—not a chat answer.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:45.000
A shorthand workout becomes a readable log.
The raw line stays attached, and every number is still mine to edit.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:56.000
When Unfiled offers an interpretation,
it labels the generated text and keeps the original close.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
It does not turn a loose attribution into historical fact.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:18.000
A follow-up can update the right living note
instead of creating another untitled fragment.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:29.000
The native app and web client share
one authenticated backend and revision history.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Search scope is explicit.
Production-gated features stay disabled until proved.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Organization is never the final authority.
Every change is inspectable, correctable, and reversible.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Unfiled—synthetic portfolio demonstration.
Public-beta gates are still being completed.
